als and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Hawaii is among the most Democratic states in presidential elections, with a partisan lean of roughly 13 points toward Democrats and a long record of Democratic wins in the state's electoral votes. No incumbent is on the ballot in 2028, and neither party has a defined general-election nominee yet, so the race is effectively between generic party candidates.\n\nNo public polls of the Hawaii race, no expert ratings, and no market pricing are available, so the outlook rests on the state's fundamentals. Those point to a comfortable but not certain Democratic win, with the margin expected in the low double digits. A strong national Republican year could narrow it considerably, but a Republican victory would require a shift far beyond anything Hawaii's recent presidential history suggests.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8703, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9295, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8784, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.877, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8862, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.878, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8719, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8743, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8792, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.879, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8843, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8748, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8714, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8851, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.8645, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-